<h2 class="mt-12">Governance and documentation for customer service</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>Standard</th><th>Risk it prevents</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Flow ownership</td><td>One accountable customer service operator per flow</td><td>Ownerless customer service flows decaying live</td></tr>
<tr><td>Naming convention</td><td>customer service-flow names lead with purpose</td><td>customer service chaos when names carry no signal</td></tr>
<tr><td>Change log</td><td>Log customer service edits with date and rationale</td><td>customer service performance drift with no log</td></tr>
<tr><td>Access control</td><td>customer service access scoped to role</td><td>customer service rogue sends from open permissions</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quarterly flow review</td><td>Simplify dormant customer service paths</td><td>customer service cruft raising edit cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>Incident runbook</td><td>Customer Service incident path: pause, notify, fix</td><td>Slow customer service kill on broken sends</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Peak season readiness for customer service</h2>
<ol>
<li>Halt customer service edits ahead of the peak window.</li>
<li>For customer service, trial every journey against real order events.</li>
<li>Verify customer service suppression clears recent buyers and open returns.</li>
<li>Enlarge customer service holdouts so peak reads stay valid.</li>
<li>Set customer service SMS boundaries ahead of volume.</li>
<li>Match customer service plan caps and overage rates to forecast volume.</li>
<li>For customer service, name a daily inbox-health monitor.</li>
<li>Bank customer service rollback plans ahead of sends.</li>
</ol>
<p>For customer service, schedule quarter-one review before the first send. Writing customer service suppression rules, discount caps, and escalation paths down in week one saves weeks of peak-season triage and hands newcomers a working customer service playbook.</p>
<p>Close each customer service quarter with a written ledger — customer service sends shipped, suppressions honored, margin retained, failed bets — so customer service vendor decisions rest on one shared evidence file, not scattered memory.</p>
